On/Off policy: 

Policy- the guide for an agent when it encounters different states. Involves mapping states of the environment and agent to decisions that the agent should make. These can be simple like a state resulting in a fixed action, or they can be much more complex calculations involving learning from past attempts. Goal is to have a policy such that it maximizes the reward for the agent during its run.  

 

Exploration & Exploitation 

Exploration- try new actions to gain more information and possibly more rewarding routes 

Exploitation- use current knowledge to make a choice with more immediate reward  

A trade-off between the two E’s is crucial for the effectiveness of RL algorithms  

 

On-Policy Learning 

It uses the current strategy to go through the problem and learn from its attempts. Kind of like how humans learn from trial and error. It uses its own actions to “master” its decision making.  

Off-Policy Learning 

This approach learns from watching someone else’s experience. By observing another strategy (potentially better), you can learn about the optimal policy without having to follow it. Like learning from videos experiences that you would have never encountered in your own life.  

 

Pros & Cons 

On – Is more straightforward and self-contained. But could be less efficient, spending time learning from sub-optimal actions 

Off – Could be more efficient if it is learning from good resources and optimal actions. But much more complex applying the observations into your own policy actions 

 

Markov Decision Process: 

It is used in situations where an agent needs to work through a variable environment where each action could lead to a different outcome. Agents need to know what action to take, what happens after that action, and if the result is good or bad.  

 

Five Main Parts: 

States – condition and place of an agent 

Actions – what an agent can do from its current state 

Transition Model – what happens after an action is taken 

Reward - number given after an action is taken. Positive if the action should be encouraged or negative it should be discouraged 

Policy – the agent’s plan behind taking actions in different states 

 

